<title>CHINA: China, GM's Hughes unit in satellite pact.</title>
<headline>China, GM's Hughes unit in satellite pact.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>China and General Motors Corp's Hughes Space and Communications International unit signed a long-term satellite launch agreement on Saturday, the official Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>It said that under the accord, China's Long March series of rockets would be used to launch at least five Hughes satellites with the option for five more launches.  </p>
<p>The launches would be made between the second half of 1998 and the end of 2006.</p>
<p>Xinhua said the agreement was signed between Hughes and China Great Wall Industry Corp, a state-run company that handles commercial space launch contracts with foreign companies.</p>
</text>
